<speak>I'm letting it develop a bit. If I announce a completely rigid timetable, I know I'll be the first person to break it. At home, I try to finish the necessary calls before lunch and then do something away from the desk. The main difficulty is not filling the space with more work. A quiet afternoon can look like an invitation to clear old emails. My wife says I need to practise having an afternoon, not just having fewer meetings.</speak>